You need to find probability of getting number on second roll is same as number on the first roll. That will give you probability of winning the game and for fair game you need to multiply probability of winning with an amount won by player and that should be equal to amount player pays.
Answer>\begin{aligned} &\text { Probability of getting number on second roll is same as number on the first roll}\\ &=\dfrac{1}{3}\times\dfrac{1}{6}\\ &=\dfrac{1}{18}\\ &\text { Now since it is fair game, amount prize must be such that probability of player winning} \\ &\cdot \text { times win of player is equal to an amount player pays. So} \\ &\dfrac{1}{18} \cdot winning =100\\ &\text{So, winning} = \$1800 \end{aligned}
